WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.625
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.625 --> 00:00:02.130
SPEAKER: At
Hillsdale, we believe

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:04.590
that college isn't just
something you go to,

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.740
it's something you become a part
of for the rest of your life.

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:11.040
This is why every student
beginning their journey

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.290
at Hillsdale is asked
to commit themselves

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.670
to a set of principles known
as the Freshman Pledge.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:19.020
This pledge reminds
us that college is not

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.570
a commodity, but a commitment.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.710
And it defines this relationship
between college and student,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.720
a partnership where
Hillsdale promises

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.150
not only to provide
a good education,

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:34.490
but to lead every student forth
towards a good and noble life.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.620
Through this pledge,
we commit ourselves

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.750
to diligent study and
patient reflection,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.800
to learning and living
with integrity and honor.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.910
We embrace the highest ideals
of a liberal arts education,

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:50.630
the pursuit of truth,
the love of the good,

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.150
and the cultivation of beauty.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.120
And we believe that the
pursuit of these ideals

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:00.320
will shape our minds and our
hearts for an ennobled society.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:04.250
This is the high calling
of a Hillsdale education.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.380
This is the Freshman Pledge.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

